From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:31:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: don't elide barrier syncs while u_trace is
 recording

With MESA_GPU_TRACES set, the first queue wait after a barrier lost the
device (CS_FATAL FATAL_CS_INVALID_INSTRUCTION, vkQueueWaitIdle returned
VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST) on any build with barrier sync elision. Bisected on
drawbench indep 64: builds up to and including the deferred timestamp walk
change trace fine; the build that adds barrier sync elision and idle compute
subqueue work faults, and every later build does. With
PANVK_NO_SYNC_ELISION=1 the current build traces fine.

u_trace brackets each barrier with begin/end markers whose timestamp
writes run on the subqueues the barrier waits on; with elision the compute
subqueue's waits are deferred instead of emitted, so the markers and the
deferred waits no longer line up. Tracing is a debug path whose job is to
show the barriers, so return false from panvk_cmd_sync_elision_enabled()
while u_trace is enabled: traced command buffers get the plain barriers,
untraced ones are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: debug tooling: MESA_GPU_TRACES (u_trace) no longer loses the device; barrier sync elision (rg477m/009) is turned off while u_trace is recording, untraced command buffers are unchanged
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: applies after rg477m/045; fixes the u_trace interaction of rg477m/009
Validation test: drawbench indep 64 with MESA_GPU_TRACES=print: rg477m/001-045 FATAL_CS_INVALID_INSTRUCTION + VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST (bisected: 001-008 fine, 001-009 faults), with this patch runs (1.92 ms/frame); without tracing drawbench indep 64 unchanged (1.00-1.05 ms/frame both builds); rg046-compat (b85e6945ab6c, rg477m/001-046): PanProbe 38/38 x2; validate-series --build: 219 patches apply, tree identical, 0 warnings
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h
index 4a321536..038cf982 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h
@@ -841,6 +841,12 @@ panvk_cmd_sync_elision_enabled(const struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
    if (disabled < 0)
       disabled = debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_NO_SYNC_ELISION", false);
 
+   /* Elided barriers lose the device under u_trace (its barrier and timestamp
+    * instructions don't follow the deferred compute waits). Tracing is a
+    * debug path: trace the unelided barriers. */
+   if (u_trace_enabled(cmdbuf->utrace.uts[0].utctx))
+      return false;
+
    return !disabled && cmdbuf->vk.level == VK_COMMAND_BUFFER_LEVEL_PRIMARY;
 }
 
